# DESCRIPTION

Text in `libvx` is a slice, `vx_str`: UTF-8 that carries its length and is never NUL-terminated (09 §3, ADR-0013); `VX_STR("lit")` makes one from a literal, and `vx_cstr` from a C string.
Offsets are in bytes. Every call here but `vx_printf` and `vx_eprintf` is pure: no call to the kernel (M6 step 6e4c2).

`vx_str_cut` is the bytes <from> to <to> of <s>, each clamped to its length.
`vx_str_find` is where <needle> first starts in <s>, or -1.
`vx_str_split` takes the next field of <*s> up to <sep> into <*field> and moves <*s> past it, and is false once <*s> is used up: `"a,b,"` gives `a`, `b` and an empty field.
`vx_str_u64` reads decimal digits, or `0x` and hex digits; `vx_str_i64` also takes a sign; both are false, leaving <*out> alone, for anything else or a number that does not fit.
`vx_str_cat` joins <n> slices in arena <a>; `VX_STR_CAT(a, x, y, ...)` takes them as a list.

The formatting calls take printf's verbs, so clang checks every format against its arguments.
A slice prints as `"%.*s", VX_FMT(s)`.
`vx_fmt` formats into arena <a>; like `vx_str_cat`, the result is followed by a NUL its length does not count, and is the zero slice if the arena is full.
`vx_bfmt` formats into <buf> as much as fits, cut at a rune's boundary, with no NUL, and returns how many bytes that is.
`vx_printf` writes to standard output and `vx_eprintf` to standard error, each in one write, so a program's threads do not interleave within one; each returns how many bytes, or a negative `vx_status`.
`vx_vfmt` and `vx_vbfmt` take a `va_list`.

The verbs are C's: flags `-+ #0`, a width and a precision, either of which may be `*`, the lengths `hh h l ll j z t L`, and `d i u o x X b B c s p f F e E g G a A %`.
Floating point is exact: a double is expanded to all its decimal digits and rounded half to even, so the output is glibc's, byte for byte (`tests/host/text_test.c` compares a million formats).

# EXAMPLES

```c
vx_str line = VX_STR("name=disk0 size=1048576"), field;
while (vx_str_split(&line, VX_STR(" "), &field))
  if (vx_str_prefix(field, VX_STR("size="))) {
    uint64_t size;
    if (vx_str_u64(vx_str_cut(field, 5, field.len), &size))
      vx_printf("%.1f MiB\n", size / 1048576.0);
  }
```

